        <p>I bars just. reed • Very illterelitlng an4Rignifintot injunction to the branchen ol the Primrose League The officiais bale rout, it nemeotary to state that on on Recount should children be allowed to sign a solemn declaratlon until they are old enough to uottorm•od it, meaning, end, further, that t. the Mwtomary age of adliniwien as full member is six- teen or Deventeen.- When younger than Om, the ' members are dubbed " Primrow Buds. No limit seems to be placed to the youth of o bud!'</p>
        <p>The perils .4 greatnase are, indeed, alarming. It I is reported from the Cape t tat ° a now honour " threatens Mr. Rhodes. It is no lees than • proposal that " during this moment°,ta cr.., in Its, We," the fond parents of newlysarnsuid colonists should name them after the great Cecil. Not content with this, the originator of this brilliant ides further lugged' that the portraits of these intereeting bahn should be collected in an album and presented to Mr Rhodes, who is, as all the world knows • bachelor.</p>
